WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.467
- So how do you go

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.233
Ah ha!

00:00:02.233 --> 00:00:03.734
How do you think?

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:12.000
What happened?
You're rubbing your head.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.900
Oh, no.
Right here is just aching.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:14.800
It is?

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.700
Yeah, I don't know why.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.033
Is it the conversation?

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.266
Like my brain is
just so excited.

00:00:20.266 --> 00:00:21.500
Your brain is so excited?

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.567
Yeah.

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:23.934
I've never met an
astronaut in my life.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.233
Really?

00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:27.133
Yeah, have you ever
tried any space food?

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.033
Um, no.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:31.967
What was the strangest thing
that happened to you in space?

00:00:31.967 --> 00:00:33.834
Just about everything
is different.

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:36.734
You see things that
you know what they are,

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:40.133
but you haven't seen them
in that perspective before.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:41.734
But while your space
walking-- which

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:44.300
is your question-- what do you
do if you go to the bathroom?

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.166
You wear diapers.

00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:47.433
What do you think of that?

00:00:47.433 --> 00:00:49.200
Just like when we were babies.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.200
Adults are babies?

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.734
Adults are babies now.

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:54.166
Like if you're trying
to fix something,

00:00:54.166 --> 00:00:57.467
did you ever let go
of it and it flew off?

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:59.100
What do you think
we could do to try

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.900
to prevent the from happening?

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.367
Glue your hand to it?

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.567
What your favorite
food on earth?

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:05.700
Pizza.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:06.633
Pizza?

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.200
Yeah, that's the
one thing we can't

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.767
get in space when I was flying.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:13.533
But now, for the first time,
you can even eat pizza in space.

00:01:13.533 --> 00:01:15.567
How did you
become an astronaut?

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:18.367
Well, you have to apply
to become a astronaut.

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:19.667
Astronaut schools?

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.266
And then I had to go
to astronaut school.

00:01:21.266 --> 00:01:23.633
And I applied and I got
rejected three times.

00:01:23.633 --> 00:01:24.867
Took me 10 years.

00:01:24.867 --> 00:01:27.233
When I grow up, I actually
want to be an engineer.

00:01:27.233 --> 00:01:28.834
And I heard you're one.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:31.166
So can you give me some
tip on some things?

00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:33.900
Just to keep your
curiosity going about things,

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.900
and learn as much as you can.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:40.800
And it's going to get harder
and harder, so just keep at it.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.500
[music playing]

